# The image installs its own dependencies and builds its own output, so
# nothing from the host's is sent to the builder. Above all not a local
# `.env`, in an app or a package: Next loads an app's when present, and they
# hold secrets. BuildKit reads this file in place of a root `.dockerignore`
# because it sits beside the Dockerfile, so the starter export carries
# neither.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.playwright
**/out
**/dist
**/.mail
**/.mail-e2e
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.git
.DS_Store
